From dcb6019b1bfa57a046583b386220581e90697ba8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:10:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aegisos: fix legacy power-menu fallback to use
 getUsersForUiDisplay

LegacyGlobalActions is a live fallback path (used when SystemUI fails
to respond to the power-menu request within 5s, or reports
onGlobalActionsAvailableChanged(false)), not dead code. Its
addUsersToMenu() called the raw, unfiltered UserManager#getUsers() and
rendered every real user's name with a checkmark directly on the lock
screen (showDuringKeyguard()=true) -- a real leak found during an
exhaustive audit of every getUsers()-style call site after a related
leak (ADR-066) turned out not to be isolated.

Fixed by routing through getUsersForUiDisplay(true), the same
decoy-aware primitive every other Component B fix in this feature
already uses.
---
 .../java/com/android/server/policy/LegacyGlobalActions.java | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/LegacyGlobalActions.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/LegacyGlobalActions.java
index d83d7f17a46b..c5f766e74e77 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/LegacyGlobalActions.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/LegacyGlobalActions.java
@@ -549,7 +549,11 @@ class LegacyGlobalActions implements DialogInterface.OnDismissListener, DialogIn
     private void addUsersToMenu(ArrayList<Action> items) {
         UserManager um = (UserManager) mContext.getSystemService(Context.USER_SERVICE);
         if (um.isUserSwitcherEnabled()) {
-            List<UserInfo> users = um.getUsers();
+            // getUsers() would show every real user's name on the lock screen (this menu
+            // renders with showDuringKeyguard()=true) even during an AegisOS Duress Unlock
+            // decoy session; getUsersForUiDisplay() collapses to just the decoy's own entry
+            // when the decoy is the device's actual current user.
+            List<UserInfo> users = um.getUsersForUiDisplay(true);
             UserInfo currentUser = getCurrentUser();
             for (final UserInfo user : users) {
                 if (user.isUiSwitchableHumanUser()) {
